<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna C-surface normalization: a boolean-context comparison against zero
    renders in truthy form - `if (x != 0)` as `if (x)` and `if (p == 0)` as
    `if (!p)` (user-reported readability issue on the angr fmt corpus binary:
    `if (v8 != (char *)0x0)`; no upstream GH issue).

    Upstream Ghidra always renders the explicit comparison.  kuna adds the
    settable option `truthycond` (DIV-36, docs/history.md), default-on:
    the printer marks boolean contexts (if/while/for/ternary conditions,
    &&/||/! operands) with a CONDITION_CONTEXT mod and elides the eligible
    zero operand at INT_EQUAL/INT_NOTEQUAL.  Float compares, enum-typed and
    equate-named zeros keep the explicit form; value uses never rewrite.

    Stage model: S9 emission / condition-form policy.  P0 assertion:
    `option truthycond on|off`.

    tfn (0x100000): int4 tfn(int4 x) { if (x) return 7; return 3; }
      test edi,edi / jz +6 / mov eax,7 / ret / mov eax,3 / ret
    pfn (0x100020): int4 pfn(int8 *p) { if (!p) return 1; return *p; }
      test rdi,rdi / jnz +6 / mov eax,1 / ret / mov eax,[rdi] / ret

    Pass 1 (default): `if (x)` and `if (!p)` (asserts #1-#2, exactly once
    each; the explicit forms cannot match the truthy patterns).
    Pass 2 (option truthycond off): the explicit `if (x != 0)` and - with
    the DIV-34 NULL default - `if (p == NULL)` (asserts #3-#4).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
85ff7406b807000000c3b803000000c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100020" readonly="true">
4885ff7506b801000000c38b07c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="tfn"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100020" name="pfn"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern int4 tfn(int4 x);</com>
  <com>parse line extern int4 pfn(int8 *p);</com>
  <com>lo fu tfn</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu pfn</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option truthycond off</com>
  <com>lo fu tfn</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu pfn</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CNORM-TRUTHY #1: default renders the nonzero test truthy (DIV-36)" min="1" max="1">if \(x\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CNORM-TRUTHY #2: default renders the null test as a negation" min="1" max="1">if \(!p\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CNORM-TRUTHY #3: truthycond off restores the explicit != 0" min="1" max="1">if \(x != 0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CNORM-TRUTHY #4: truthycond off restores the explicit NULL compare (DIV-34 form)" min="1" max="1">if \(p == NULL\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
